<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Product care</h2>
<p>Decide whether each message provides required order service or offers optional care education or promotion. Record the permission or other applicable basis for its purpose and channel; a purchase or SMS opt-in does not by itself authorize email marketing. Recheck current permission, suppression, order, inventory, ownership and case state before dispatch, including messages already queued.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>No documented marketing permission</td><td>Hold optional product-care promotion until eligibility is established; send required service under its applicable basis</td><td>Service eligibility does not grant promotional permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Offer relevant product education within the recorded purpose and channel</td><td>Permission alone does not establish compatibility or stock</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Check recovery eligibility and current cart state before a reminder</td><td>A cart event alone is not permission to send</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Exit recovery for the matching cart or order; reassess ownership before later eligible product-care suggestions</td><td>A purchase should stop obsolete recovery without blocking needed care</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Pause conflicting promotion and route required case service separately; reassess after resolution</td><td>Case closure alone does not restore marketing permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Review reliable clicks, purchases, complaints and a documented sunset policy</td><td>Non-opens alone do not reliably establish inactivity</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Verify its purpose, region, quiet hours, caps and current withdrawal state separately</td><td>SMS permission does not transfer to email</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Verify recipient role, purpose and applicable channel eligibility</td><td>An account relationship is not blanket promotional permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Use address validity, permission and abuse evidence; do not reject a free domain alone</td><td>Domain type alone does not establish consent or deliverability</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Exclude test profiles from production audiences and measurement</td><td>Internal activity can distort program metrics</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Apply the same documented eligibility rules</td><td>Inferred identity does not override permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Hold promotion while checking available evidence; seek repermission only through an independently permitted route</td><td>A request for consent is itself a message requiring eligibility</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Product care</h2>
<p>Product Care profit needs the whole ledger: subscription plus overages, SMS credits, capture and template spend, agency retainers, and product care discount margin against attributed revenue. Product Care rule: near fifteen percent stack-to-margin, cut product care complexity before chasing gains.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. Free tiers ration contacts, sends, branching, or support — confirm which ceiling binds your product care plan first.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Cost component</th><th>What to model</th><th>Common failure</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Platform subscription</td><td>Tier your product care plan to contacts you truly hold</td><td>product care plan sized for hopes, not contacts</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contact or send overages</td><td>Map product care list growth to tier thresholds</td><td>Product Care seasonal spikes surprise-billing</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS credits</td><td>Scale product care SMS by opt-ins and journey length</td><td>product care text costs wished into email costs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Discount budget</td><td>Price product care incentives by redemption probability</td><td>product care incentives training perpetual waiting</td></tr>
<tr><td>Creative and ops time</td><td>Operator hours the product care program consumes weekly</td><td>product care maintenance hours wished away</td></tr>
